{
  // Typechecks the test files `tsconfig.json` excludes from the BUILD (that
  // exclusion is load-bearing: without it, tests would be emitted into `dist`
  // and published). `noEmit` makes this config incapable of writing to `dist`.
  //
  // `*.test-d.ts(x)` stays out: `pnpm test:types` already runs those
  // through vitest's typecheck mode against the built `dist`.
  //
  // `src/__tests__/fixtures/**` IS included. Those are standalone mini-apps
  // compiled by a CHILD Vite process, and the framework imports they make
  // (`hono-preact`, the umbrella) are supplied to that process by each
  // fixture's `resolve.alias`, because the umbrella is deliberately unreachable
  // from `packages/vite` (depending on it would be a circular workspace edge).
  // `paths` below is tsc's equivalent of that alias and needs no dependency
  // edge, so the fixtures typecheck here without one. It points at the built
  // `dist` (what a real consumer of the package resolves), which CI and the
  // documented pre-push order already build before any typecheck runs.
  //
  // The tradeoff: this is a build-order dependency that no `package.json` edge
  // declares, so `pnpm -r` cannot order it for you. Running `typecheck:tests`
  // in a fresh worktree BEFORE `pnpm build` reports ~14 `TS2307: Cannot find
  // module 'hono-preact'` against fixture files nobody touched. Build first.
  // Note `tsconfig.json` (the emitting config) deliberately has no `paths`, so
  // a non-fixture `src` file still cannot name the umbrella.
  //
  // Everything else the fixtures import (`@hono-preact/iso`, `hono`, `preact`,
  // `vite`, ...) is a real dependency of this package and resolves normally.
  "extends": "./tsconfig.json",
  "compilerOptions": {
    "noEmit": true,
    "paths": {
      "hono-preact": ["../hono-preact/dist/index.d.ts"],
      "hono-preact/*": ["../hono-preact/dist/*"]
    }
  },
  "include": ["src/**/*.ts", "src/**/*.tsx"],
  "exclude": ["src/**/*.test-d.ts", "src/**/*.test-d.tsx"]
}
